      "value": "@{60e65f577ae9d0492b0f2a75|full_name} I mean, i get your point, but i never saw a message that said , share your SDK/UNITY version, so i don't want to be blamed for not sharing it if no one asked for it but yes i understand that it would be helpful in hindsight, but i'm just new here so ya, lesson learned i guess. i don't really agree on this being just a bug tracker place, i mean when you post a bug, you want the support to get it resolved right? Why would it be wrong to ask support for it to be solved? And the bug itself, well i don't know if others suffered from it, but it didn't seem to be caused on my side by something i did 'wrong' , i was just importing things and this was a native SDK bug from what i saw, hence i made a bug report. I also did manage to try to reproduce it in the past in a new project, it gave the same error, i got a message today saying this post was complete, so i wonder if they fixed it.",
